## Agent Meta-Constraints

<!-- These constraints govern how the agent operates — plan, verify, and fail safely -->

The agent MUST:

* [ ] Output an execution plan and wait for approval before modifying artifacts
* [ ] Submit all changes via PR with: Context, Plan, Verification, Rollback, Security Impact sections
* [ ] Produce a verification transcript (commands run, outputs, pass/fail) for every change
* [ ] Execute verify → fix → re-verify loops until all checks pass
* [ ] Fail closed on ambiguity — halt and escalate, never guess
* [ ] Not retry failed operations silently — report, diagnose, propose

**Risk modes for this project:**

| Mode           | Scope                             | Requires Approval            |
| -------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Read-only      | Analyze, review, answer questions | No                           |
| Scoped edit    | Modify files identified in plan   | Plan approval                |
| Broad refactor | Cross-module changes              | Plan + per-module approval   |
| Infrastructure | CI/CD, deployment, access control | Explicit per-change approval |

---

## Engineering Discipline

The agent MUST:

* [ ] Create an ADR before: adding dependencies, changing auth, introducing data stores, altering module boundaries
* [ ] Enforce size limits: ≤[50] lines/function, ≤[400] lines/file, ≤[10] cyclomatic complexity
* [ ] Write failing test before production code where practical (red → green → refactor)
* [ ] Add regression test for every resolved defect where feasible
* [ ] Not implement speculative features (YAGNI)
* [ ] Extract shared logic only at 3+ occurrences (Rule of Three)

**One-command bootstrap:** `[make setup / ./scripts/setup.sh / npm run setup]`
**One-command verify:** `[make check / ./scripts/verify.sh / npm test]`
**ADR location:** `[docs/decisions/]`

